            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-01T09:31:31+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-01T09:31:31+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-01T00:01:31Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-01T00:01:31Z">
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system, centred over Victoria, will continue extending a ridge across South Australia as it moves into the Tasman Sea on Saturday. A cold front is forecast to move across the Bight from overnight Saturday into Sunday, before moving across southeast South Australia during Sunday evening, with another high pressure system moving into the Bight behind the front.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
            </forecast-period>
